]


The two local models show no consistent pattern: in Qwen3 a stated strengthener widened the spread (+2.6 points) and a weakener narrowed it (−2.1), so the average barely moves, and after a report the spread was smaller, not larger; in OLMo-2 the changes were near zero. The five configurations accessed through agent harnesses behave alike: after a stated update the spread narrowed by 10%–18% of the prior spread (mainly after weakeners in the four extension configurations), and after a report it was 6%–11% wider than after the same update stated (the interval excludes zero in four of the five). In claude-sonnet-5.5 and both gemini-3.8-flash configurations, items with a more dispersed prior also moved more (ρ = 0.24 to 0.31); in the other four configurations the correlation was weak (0.08 to 0.15) and its interval included zero. These are small absolute differences (under 2 points of spread) and were examined only post hoc. In the harnessed configurations the candidate spread thus shows the pattern one would expect of an expression of uncertainty (narrowing with information, staying wider for hearsay), whereas in the two small local models it does not show this pattern; there is no independent measure of uncertainty against which to check either, and those seven configurations alone cannot separate model scale, harnesses, and training; the API extension below tests whether a harness is necessary.

The raw REST API results show that stated narrowing followed by reported widening does not require a CLI harness: four of eight formal API configurations show both signs (@tab-spread). Gemini Flash-Lite gives −22.7% / +22.6%, Gemma 31B −13.3% / +7.6%, Gemma 26B-A4B −6.6% / +6.4%, and GLM 9B −5.4% / +8.4%. The dev ladder (@tab-api-dev) also includes this pattern on groq:gpt-oss-120b (−18.4% / +12.2%), nv:nemotron-3-ultra-550b (−21.4% / +14.1%), nv:nemotron-3.5-super-vl-120b (−17.5% / +3.3%), and ms:qwen3.5-27b (−14.0% / +11.7%).

Four candidate factors emerge as exploratory, post-hoc empirical associations across the 15 formal and 20 dev configurations:

+ #strong[Total and active scale within families.] On Groq, gpt-oss-120b gives −18.4% / +12.2%, versus +4.3% / +3.3% for gpt-oss-20b. Formal Gemma 31B dense shows twice the stated narrowing of 4B-active Gemma MoE. Large total size is insufficient: 29B dense sf:xing4.0-29b gives −4.3% / −4.2%.
+ #strong[MoE routing capacity.] Nemotron 30B-A3B gives +8.0% / −9.3%, whereas 120B-A12B and 550B-A55B show both expected signs. These contrasts vary absolute active scale as well as active-to-total ratio and do not isolate routing causally.
+ #strong[Family and instruction-tuning generation.] On SiliconFlow, Qwen2.5 7B widens on both contrasts (+4.7% / +3.5%); Qwen3 8B narrows on both (−2.4% / −6.2%), matching local Qwen3’s reported contrast (−13%); GLM 9B shows both expected signs. Similar size does not imply similar spread behavior.
+ #strong[Reasoning and weight-field burden.] Gemini low/high effort show similar stated narrowing (−17% / −15%), with somewhat more reported widening at high effort (+11% vs. +6%). Removing the Weight field in the OpenAI ablation (V2; Section 4.9) reduces within-call SD from 15.23 / 22.26 to 6.59 / 7.85 points.

These associations have exceptions, and provider, family, post-training and calling settings remain confounded. They motivate controlled tests rather than a causal ranking of factors.

== Un-harnessed REST API extension (dnli-api)

The eight formal API configurations yield 11,188/11,200 valid units (99.89%). Each has 120 Block-A pairs and 20 repeat pairs. H1 and H4a reject in all eight. Seven reject H2; sf:qwen3.5-4b does not. Even sf:xing4.0-29b rejects its one-sided H2 test under Holm despite its two-sided 95% interval spanning zero. Together with the primary and CLI extension studies, H1 and H4a reject in all 15 formal configurations and H2 in 13 of 15.

