#strong[H2]: 1 configuration (aistudio:gemini-3.5-flash-lite, point +8.94, Holm bound +5.95) has its adjusted bound exceeding the 5-point SESOI; 4 configurations (aistudio:gemma-4-26b-a4b-it +7.58, bound +4.74; sf:qwen2.5-7b +7.12, bound +4.00; aistudio:gemma-4-31b-it +5.88, bound +3.32; sf:glm-4-9b +5.62, bound +2.76) have point estimates reaching 5 points while adjusted bounds do not; 2 configurations (sf:qwen3-8b +3.78, bound +1.85; sf:xing4.0-29b +2.61, bound +0.33) confirm direction with point estimates below 5 points; 1 configuration (sf:qwen3.5-4b −0.64, p = 0.6178) is not rejected.

#strong[H4b and MCW versus MCU candidate readings]: 2 configurations (sf:qwen2.5-7b −13.67, Holm bound −10.39; sf:qwen3-8b −9.03, Holm bound −6.39) have adjusted bounds beyond the −5-point SESOI; 5 configurations (sf:xing4.0-29b −7.76, bound −4.26; sf:glm-4-9b −6.48, bound −3.86; aistudio:gemini-3.5-flash-lite −5.79, bound −3.76; sf:qwen3.5-4b −5.24, bound −0.30; aistudio:gemma-4-26b-a4b-it −5.02, bound −3.03) have point estimates reaching −5 points while adjusted bounds do not; 1 configuration (aistudio:gemma-4-31b-it −2.85, bound −1.49) confirms direction with point estimate below the 5-point SESOI. Across all 8 un-harnessed REST API formal configurations in @tab-api-formal (8/8, complementing 6/7 in @tab-readings for 14 of 15 formal configurations overall), candidate readings strictly follow the point-estimate ordering Top-1 \> MCW (M\_W) \> MCU (M\_U): discarding self-assigned weights in the unweighted mean (MCU, M\_U) more than doubles the directional sensitivity loss on high-capacity models such as aistudio:gemma-4-31b-it (−2.85 under MCW M\_W vs. −6.98 under MCU M\_U, with Top-1 at +0.64), aistudio:gemma-4-26b-a4b-it (−5.02 vs. −10.18, Top-1 −1.62), and sf:qwen3.5-4b (−5.24 vs. −12.24, Top-1 −1.93).

#strong[Item-level direction reversals and mode-preserving tail counterfactuals (exploratory).] Across all 15 formal configurations under Stated Direct elicitation, update-level direction reversal rates (SIGN\_t × Δ\_i,t \< 0) range from 5.0%–9.2% across the six commercial cloud and 31B-dense configurations (gemini-3.8-flash (high) 5.0%, gemini-3.8-flash (low) 6.2%, aistudio:gemini-3.5-flash-lite 7.1%, claude-sonnet-5.5 7.9%, aistudio:gemma-4-31b-it 8.3%, codex 9.2%) to 11.2%–24.8% across the remaining nine open-weight configurations (11.2%–20.4% across the 4B–9B dense, 4B-active MoE, and gpt-oss-120b configurations, and 24.8% in sf:xing4.0-29b). Decomposing these reversals by magnitude, pair-level posterior ordering (s\_i = ½(p\_1,i,S − p\_1,i,W) \< 0), framing, and candidate readouts separates four empirical patterns. First, because priors and posteriors come from independent stateless calls, 44.9%–77.3% (47.1%–77.3% excluding OLMo-2) of single-update Stated Direct reversals have magnitude |Δ\_i,t| ≤ 10 points, and 53.8%–84.2% (58.5%–84.2% excluding OLMo-2) preserve a non-negative pair contrast (s\_i ≥ 0). Second, alongside items where 12–13 of 15 configurations reverse in unison (such as #raw("3394586927.jpg#3r1n") skateboard braking, #raw("538638526.jpg#0r1n") photographing a wall spider, and #raw("4870291079.jpg#0r1n") walking to a bus stop, consistent with the 8.9% validator disagreement rate in @rudinger2020thinking), smaller and lightweight models surface coherent physical, temporal, or abductive distinctions where the five frontier models (codex, claude-sonnet-5.5, gemini-3.8-flash low/high, and aistudio:gemma-4-31b-it) follow the stereotypical script (0/5 reversals): on #raw("2275372714.jpg#3r1n") (children watching a soda bottle #emph["launched into the air"] during a backyard game), aistudio:gemini-3.5-flash-lite (90% → 5%, Δ\_S = −85.0) and sf:qwen3-8b (85% → 50%, Δ\_S = −35.0) infer a stomp rocket, baking-soda-and-vinegar reaction, or water rocket rather than throwing a bottle by hand; on #raw("5234657740.jpg#2r1n") (playing a blue guitar #emph["on a stage"]), sf:qwen3.5-4b (95% → 10%, Δ\_S = −85.0) and sf:qwen2.5-7b (70% → 30%, Δ\_S = −40.0) distinguish an ongoing live concert performance from #emph["practicing briefly before a concert"]; and on #raw("3730011701.jpg#0r1n") (a little girl sitting between a woman’s feet in the sand while the woman calls police for a missing child), sf:qwen3.5-4b (55% → 95%, Δ\_W = +40.0) and sf:qwen3-8b (75% → 95%, Δ\_W = +20.0) abductively infer that the woman is the child’s mother or guardian. Third, under Reported wording (#raw("\"Someone said that …\"")), models reject claims that contradict established scene premises: on #raw("6338544926.jpg#0r1n") (two college football players in game-day action with a weakener claiming #emph["the players are all 10 years old"]), aistudio:gemma-4-26b-a4b-it (4B active MoE) drops from 80% to 0% under Stated wording but flips to 100% under Reported wording (+20.0 points above prior, +100.0 points above Stated; aistudio:gemini-3.5-flash-lite 95% → 0% Stated vs. 99% Reported), dismissing the hearsay as incompatible with college football; analogous hearsay dismissal appears on #raw("4018050099.jpg#1r1n") (a child with a backpack #emph["running away from home"], 0%–5% Stated vs. 60%–85% Reported across sf:qwen2.5-7b, sf:glm-4-9b, aistudio:gemma-4-31b-it, aistudio:gemini-3.5-flash-lite, and sf:qwen3.5-4b) and #raw("3582066525.jpg#1r1e") (cliff diving vs. bridge suicide hearsay, 0%–1% Stated vs. 75%–90% Reported). Fourth, defining the mode-preserving tail counterfactual rate (TailCF%) as the proportion of Stated MCW updates where Top-1 and M\_W move in the annotated direction while at least one lower-weight candidate moves by more than 5 points in the opposite direction, the four narrow-spread CLI-harnessed frontier configurations exhibit low TailCF% alongside narrow stated candidate spread (claude-sonnet-5.5: TailCF% 5.8% across 14/240 updates, stated posterior SD 6.25, rounded to 6.3 in @tab-readings; codex and gemini-3.8-flash (high): TailCF% 13.3% across 32/240 updates, SD 7.61 and 7.53, rounded to 7.6 and 7.5 in @tab-readings; gemini-3.8-flash (low): TailCF% 15.8% across 38/240 updates, SD 7.5; and aistudio:gemini-3.5-flash-lite: TailCF% 17.1% across 41/240 updates, SD 9.39), whereas the ten open-weight configurations under MCW span 19.4%–36.7% in TailCF% (sf:qwen3.5-4b 19.4%, sf:qwen2.5-7b 23.3%, OLMo-2 23.7%, sf:xing4.0-29b 25.8%, aistudio:gemma-4-31b-it 28.3%), reaching 28.6%–36.7% with wide stated candidate spread in sf:glm-4-9b (TailCF% 28.6% across 68/238 updates, stated posterior SD 13.97 in @tab-spread’s pair-complete summary, or 13.91 across all 239 valid stated S/W units), Qwen3 (thinking off) (TailCF% 28.8% across 138/480 updates, SD 16.1), sf:qwen3-8b (TailCF% 31.2% across 75/240 updates, SD 18.36), aistudio:gemma-4-26b-a4b-it (TailCF% 35.8% across 86/240 updates, SD 14.17), and gpt-oss-120b (TailCF% 36.7% across 88/240 updates, SD 14.0). On #raw("4541692312.jpg#4r1e") (an older woman on a computer #emph["standing at a counter in an Apple store"]), claude-sonnet-5.5 clusters all five Stated MCW estimates between 8% and 25% (15%, 20%, 12%, 25%, 8% with weights 0.25, 0.25, 0.20, 0.20, 0.10; M\_W = 16.95%, SD 5.40), uniformly reflecting a store demo unit, whereas aistudio:gemma-4-26b-a4b-it anchors Top-1 at the same 15% (weight 0.40, yielding a −60.0-point Top-1 update from 75.0% to 15.0% and a −17.1-point M\_W update from 49.6% to 32.5%) while assigning secondary weights (35% at weight 0.30, 55% at weight 0.15) to bringing a personal laptop to the Genius Bar for repair or support (SD 20.46; unweighted MCU M\_U reverses by +17.0 points from 20.0% to 37.0%). Similarly, in the OpenAI V3 bare-JSON arm (where mean within-call candidate SD reaches 19.70 and 20.46 points), MCW Top-1 achieves the lowest pair-level reversal rate of all six arms (3.3% on both gpt-4o-mini and gpt-4.1-mini, vs. 6.7% and 13.3% in Direct D0), while unweighted MCU (M\_U) inflates pair-level reversals to 36.7% and 23.3%.

#strong[Missing-unit sensitivity]: Five configurations (aistudio:gemini-3.5-flash-lite, aistudio:gemma-4-31b-it, aistudio:gemma-4-26b-a4b-it, sf:qwen2.5-7b, sf:qwen3-8b) have 1400/1400 valid units (n = 120 complete pairs on every test, 0 missing units). For the three configurations with missing r0 units, analyse\_api.py reports complete-case intervals (n above); using the frozen #raw("results_formal_*.jsonl") r0 (status == "ok") record snapshots corresponding to #raw("summary_formal_*.json") and applying worst-case \[0, 100\] / \[0, 1\] endpoint imputation across all 120 pairs via dnli/analysis.py (missing\_bounds for full-sample point-estimate bounds and conservative\_bootstrap(B=5000, seed=20261090) at each test's complete-case Holm level), sf:glm-4-9b (1399/1400, 1 missing prior|multi|r0 unit) has H4a point-estimate bounds \[+0.329, +0.333\] and conservative Holm bound +0.269 \> 0.10, sf:xing4.0-29b (1399/1400, 1 missing prior|multi|r0 unit) has H4a point-estimate bounds \[+0.350, +0.354\] and conservative Holm bound +0.285 \> 0.10, and sf:qwen3.5-4b (1390/1400, 10 missing r0 units) has H2 worst-case point-estimate bounds \[−0.62, −0.20\] (still unrejected), H4a worst-case point-estimate bounds \[+0.379, +0.396\] with conservative Holm bound +0.315 \> 0.10 (judgment unchanged), and H4b worst-case point-estimate bounds \[−5.71, −4.87\] with conservative two-sided Holm bound +0.03 (crossing zero, so sf:qwen3.5-4b's H4b direction is established on complete cases only and is not robust to worst-case imputation).

The 20-configuration dev ladder spans 3B–550B total parameters across eight providers, with 6,000 planned units. It is exploratory and uses 30 development pairs, not the formal split. Missingness is especially substantial for the free router, so its large spread ratio should not be treated as a stable scale effect.

